Reverse Proxy
A reverse proxy sits between clients and your application servers, and
forwards requests on their behalf. It is a single, controlled entry point
(the “edge”).
• TLS termination, request routing, static asset serving.
• Caching, compression, rate limiting, access control.
• It hides how many application instances exist behind it.
