Load Balancer
A load balancer distributes incoming requests across multiple identical
instances of your application.
• Lets you scale horizontally (see the Quality Attributes class:
scalability/elasticity).
• Improves availability: if one instance dies, traffic routes to the
others.
• Most reverse proxies can act as a load balancer.
