Statelessness
For a load balancer to send a request to any instance, all instances
must behave identically. This means the application must be
stateless:
• No user session stored in the instance’s memory.
• No uploaded files stored on the instance’s local disk.
• Any per-user or per-request state must live in shared storage
(database, cache, object store) that all instances reach.
If you stored state locally in earlier assignments, you will have to
change it now.
